## THE DONE RULE (C-79; quote it from the file, at write time, exactly)
The product owner's words, `CLARIFICATIONS.md:1714`: *"Done means merged to main, the same as Composer"*. **The test, `CLARIFICATIONS.md:1716` (C-79 `Settles:`), recorded there as the coordinator's reading of the ruling, not the product owner's words:** "a ticket moves to Done when its change is merged to main AND each Done-when clause of the ticket is MET; a clause that needs a deploy, a words approval or a further ruling is still not met by a merge (B987's nine held keys are this reading: MPSCALC-139's words approval, -162's "the HOLD lifts only by a brief after deploy", -111's red check); a merge alone never moves a ticket; the rule is silent on tickets whose work is done by a ruling or a measurement with no merged change (MPSCALC-188, -288, -295, -341 and the others B987 listed as claimed only), which stay as they are." The three conditions for a move (`CLARIFICATIONS.md:1727`, B1004 item 1), all required: (1) slot `DONE-SLOT` reads `MOVE-TO-DONE`; (2) your Done-when table (Step 4a) reads MET for every clause; (3) no gate or review line and no red run contradicts it. The readings B1004 added and you may use, each only as worded there (`:1727` (a) to (d)): (a) a clause the earlier record called open counts as MET only where a later merged change closes it and that PR's diff and its gate line, re-read, show it; (b) a point the ticket's own acceptance leaves to a separate brief is not a clause; (c) a red `ci` push run of a squash does not contradict a move when the failing test is named, is not touched by the change, is present on code main, and later squashes ran the whole suite green; (d) a residual filed as ANOTHER ticket does not by itself leave this ticket's clause unmet, unless the ticket's own acceptance names it. In Jira text the rule is cited as "the product owner's 2026-11-01 ruling that Done means merged to main", never by a card id.

